{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Day to [Bb]day, just ain’t the [F]same without you
When I’m [Cm]out there searching for the things I [Gm]need to do
We can [Bb]talk, about the [F]times we need to see
[Cm]but understand the man, I’m [Gm]tryin to be
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
There are [Eb]oceans between [Bb]us,
And I [D]cannot seem to [Gm]swim
And I [Eb]know that I Love [Bb]You,
And your [D]heart I’ve tried to [Gm]win
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I can try, and Love You from here
But distance holds the key, that unlocks the fear
All I want is our love to stay,
but every time I’ve come I have to go away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
There are roads out before me,
and I cannot take them all
With me wheels a turning forward,
your love, no more will fall
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I can tell, times to head there are,
thoughts of all our space will seem too far
So forgive me for the things I do,
and I’m sorry for the pain I put you though
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
And my heart is slowly breaking,
and your love no more is mine
It has faded with the sunset,
but in my mind we’ll always shine.
{end_of_verse}
